{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396224-people-who-read-the-technocracy-reloaded-manuscript","id":1396224,"title":"People who read the Technocracy reloaded manuscript","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-13T15:38:07-07:00","id":1396224,"title":"People who read the Technocracy reloaded manuscript","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Don't you think descriptions of the Technocratic policy regarding the vampire do contradict each other?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>However, if a vampire is actively interfering with the mission at hand, you\u2019re clear to incapacitate them. This does not mean setting them on fire or blowing their head off. Word to the wise: It\u2019s virtually impossible to beat a vampire to death with a baton. Do not, repeat, do not kill one of them without authorization\u2026 unless you have to, anyway. We will win the ensuing street war, but that\u2019s a shitload of resources that we could have put to better use.</i><br /> <br /> How destroying a single HE can possibly incite a street war? Also, according to the Six Thresholds, lone vampires are categorized as 'Target of Oppertunity'.<br /> <br /> Moreover, it does contradict with EoM regarding the were creatures.<br /> <br /> TEs: Therianthropes Entities<br /> <br /> Werewolves, werespiders, werecats, and other shit that\u2019s just as scary. Fuck. There\u2019s probably a werecockroach gang out there. Do you have enough backup? The answer will always be no.<br /> <br /> When facing TEs, cheat. Cheat your fucking ass off or you won\u2019t make it home. TEs are some sort of enhanced human mutation. Like vampires, they also end up forming small gangs, but the mean physical power of any random TE far exceeds the mean physical power of vampires. Like, they aren\u2019t \u201coff the charts\u201d-level powerful, but they\u2019re definitely on the \u201cOh, shit\u201d side.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re absolutely cleared to engage on these fuckers on sight unless otherwise informed. You absolutely should not, though. The only time you should get into a fight with a therianthrope is in a carefully planned operation.<br /> <br /> Now that I\u2019ve scared the shit out of you, I\u2019m going to let you in on an important detail. Therianthropes can be Attuned. That\u2019s right. You can pull your badge out, put the fear of Lee into them, and make them put their hackles down. To make this more official, your escalation of force goes like this: If they\u2019re hostile or otherwise an impediment to operations, Attune them.<br /> <br /> If that fails, repeat Attunement protocols while retreating. If force proves necessary, use the maximum possible force possible. Your best weapon is your brain when dealing with these things, and most operatives who try using brawn against them instead wind up getting licked off some RD\u2019s claws afterward.<br /> <br /> See? Werecritters are far more powerful than HE on average. They are also organized into packs/septs. They hunt down who hurt them. But agents of the Technocracy are 'absolutely cleared' to engage whenever wherever they ache to shoot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 06-18-2020, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:51:17-07:00","id":1396228,"title":"","content":"I can't say for sure because I haven't had a chance to read TR but I think I can take a guess at the logic for these standing orders.<br /> <br /> Vampires, if left to their own devices, are not a threat to the Union's immediate priorities. Yes, they need to be exterminated eventually for everyone's sake, but for now? They largely police themselves and their priorities are rarely openly at odds with the priorities of the Union. So, best to leave them to their business and not kick that bloody hornet's nest.<br /> <br /> Thereianthropes, werecritters, and changing breeds on the other hand? They will almost always be enemies of the Union. The garou, by and large, loath the modern world. Many breeds such as the Bastet and Gurahl are similarly inclined. The Ratkin are even more extreme then the garou. The Corax and Ananasi are more subtle by far yet enable the others and manipulate the modern world to suit their needs.<br /> <br /> Changing Breeds have priorities that are distinct from the Union's because they have such a radically different perspective on the universe. The Union will need to deal with them sooner rather then later because garou monkey-wrenchers aren't going to sit on their thumbs and wait idly.<br /> <br /> Vampires largely support the modern paradigm while changing breeds largely oppose it. That means that the changing beasts need to be dealt with sooner rather then later, while the vampires can wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T17:36:01-07:00","id":1396258,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's contradictory. The Technocracy is trying to police a dark universe for the benefit of humans and the irrationality of humans makes their job really hard. So, some policies contradict because there's what factions in the Technocracy want to do and what they can do. In addition to internal politics, since the Syndicate likes money and other conventions are more interested in what money does for their projects, there's also practically. Wasting every vampire would be nice in theory, but there are other threats out there worse than a vampire.<br /> <br /> As for killing a vampire starting a street war, well if that vampire is part of a vampire group such as the Camarilla or Sabbat and has friends, well killing them could cause all their friends who were being subtle or a low-lying problem to escalate. This contradiction thus gives the group flexibility in how it deals with vampires.<br /> <br /> Is the vampire a major immediate threat? Yes--waste it. No--figure out what it wants and contain it using resources efficiently. If you have a Nephandi-influenced Technocracy, containment will be different than a more light gray Technocracy that really wants to protect humans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T18:38:20-07:00","id":1396268,"title":"","content":"A better policy is to encourage the vampire to feast upon Sleepers you dislike and provide them slaves! Because DARK UNION.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T18:47:04-07:00","id":1396269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396224-people-who-read-the-technocracy-reloaded-manuscript?p=1396268#post1396268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A better policy is to encourage the vampire to feast upon Sleepers you dislike and provide them slaves! Because DARK UNION.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is quite Technephandi. Or vampiric.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396224-people-who-read-the-technocracy-reloaded-manuscript?p=1396258#post1396258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's contradictory. The Technocracy is trying to police a dark interpretationfor the benefit of humans and the irrationality of humans makes their job really hard. So, some policies contradict because there's what factions in the Technocracy want to do and what they can do. In addition to internal politics, since the Syndicate likes money and other conventions are more interested in what money does for their projects, there's also practically. Wasting every vampire would be nice in theory, but there are other threats out there worse than a vampire.<br /> <br /> As for killing a vampire starting a street war, well if that vampire is part of a vampire group such as the Camarilla or Sabbat and has friends, well killing them could cause all their friends who were being subtle or a low-lying problem to escalate. This contradiction thus gives the group flexibility in how it deals with vampires.<br /> <br /> Is the vampire a major immediate threat? Yes--waste it. No--figure out what it wants and contain it using resources efficiently. If you have a Nephandi-influenced Technocracy, containment will be different than a more light gray Technocracy that really wants to protect humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such interpretation still begs question - why the Technocracy don't adopt same policy to Werecritters, or other supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:19:57-07:00","id":1396276,"title":"","content":"All I'm saying is the only Methodology we can trust to get the job done is SPD.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's the only division that's winning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Such interpretation still begs question - why the Technocracy don't adopt same policy to Werecritters, or other supernaturals? </div> </div> </div>Serious answer but one of the tragedies (?) of the Technocracy is that their 400+ year war against the Traditions have taken the vast majority of their resources and they're no closer to eliminating them today than they were at the beginning of their quest. Indeed, the Traditions may actually be LARGER and MORE powerful than they ever were as disparate Crafts.<br /> <br /> One could make a serious argument Operation: Ragnarok was the one unqualified Technocracy success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-13-2020, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:35:03-07:00","id":1396282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396224-people-who-read-the-technocracy-reloaded-manuscript?p=1396276#post1396276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I'm saying is the only Methodology we can trust to get the job done is SPD.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's the only division that's winning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, SPD is no longer around.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396224-people-who-read-the-technocracy-reloaded-manuscript?p=1396276#post1396276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Serious answer but one of the tragedies (?) of the Technocracy is that their 400+ year war against the Traditions have taken the vast majority of their resources and they're no closer to eliminating them today than they were at the beginning of their quest. Indeed, the Traditions may actually be LARGER and MORE powerful than they ever were as disparate Crafts.<br /> <br /> One could make a serious argument Operation: Ragnarok was the one unqualified Technocracy success.</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly didn't read the post. Official policy of the Technocracy against Werecritters and other supernaturals are a lot more aggressive than their lackluster response against the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:42:51-07:00","id":1396283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396224-people-who-read-the-technocracy-reloaded-manuscript?p=1396282#post1396282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You clearly didn't read the post. Official policy of the Technocracy against Werecritters and other supernaturals are a lot more aggressive than their lackluster response against the vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, just feel the need to joke about the Union's hypocrisy. I imagine the werecreature response is the fact they're anti-capitalist eco-terrorists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T19:49:59-07:00","id":1396287,"title":"","content":"Maybe it is for game balance reasons? Of all the WoD critters, Vampires are the most vulnerable and easiest to defeat. Just tuen them inyo lawnchairs and leave them in sunlight. Or conjure sunlight. A very anticlimatic way to handle an antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T01:25:16-07:00","id":1396330,"title":"","content":"It could be attributed to the kneejerk reaction of seeing something that scary. Werewolves have this innate fear effect after all and a lot of tech operatives are not enlightened. At least vampires can sometimes be reasoned with or maybe some vampires bribed some low level techies skewing the reports and recommendations to favor them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T04:30:43-07:00","id":1396349,"title":"","content":"Is it more that the Technocracy knows there is a large Vampire conspiracy/grouping, that tends to be more organised and likely to respond when assaulted. The text as quoted only states<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396224-people-who-read-the-technocracy-reloaded-manuscript#post1396224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Don't you think descriptions of the Technocratic policy regarding the vampire do contradict each other?</span></span></span><br /> <i>Do not, repeat, do not kill one of them without authorization\u2026 unless you have to, anyway. We will win the ensuing street war, but that\u2019s a shitload of resources that we could have put to better use.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd read this more as, there may be long running operations dealing with Vampires - trying to track back to the heart of the conspiracy, so please don't mess it up, ask before you engage. However werecreatures are not as organised - as in large deep conspiracy - and tend to be more impulsive so are fine to deal with.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T13:58:25-07:00","id":1396484,"title":"","content":"Here's my personal take on the issue: if the technocracy is sort of the FBI/CIA then vampires are the mafia/organized crime and TEs are terrorists/guerrilla fighters. It's much easier and practical to make deals or at least reach an understanding with criminals (don't cause too much trouble and I will leave you alone, also if you do me the occasional favor I will do the same for you). The main issue with organized crime is that it's, well... organized, and also exists within public and private organizations, from a cost/price in resources point of view a direct conflict is not worth the effort. Terrorists and guerrilla fighters are, as a general rule, fanatics who believe violence to be the answer to all their problems and want to disrupt the status quo no matter what. It's almost impossible to make a deal with someone like that and since destruction is their main objective you are left with no choice but to meet firepower with overwhelming firepower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T18:31:57-07:00","id":1396572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396224-people-who-read-the-technocracy-reloaded-manuscript?p=1396349#post1396349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it more that the Technocracy knows there is a large Vampire conspiracy/grouping, that tends to be more organised and likely to respond when assaulted. The text as quoted only states<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd read this more as, there may be long running operations dealing with Vampires - trying to track back to the heart of the conspiracy, so please don't mess it up, ask before you engage. However werecreatures are not as organised - as in large deep conspiracy - and tend to be more impulsive so are fine to deal with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}